---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ContactCta from "../components/ContactCta.astro";

const aboutJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ProfilePage",
  "@id": "https://maurizioturatti.com/about/#profile",
  url: "https://maurizioturatti.com/about/",
  name: "About Maurizio Turatti",
  description:
    "Over two decades of making technical decisions and living with the consequences. Architecture advice grounded in direct experience building and operating software.",
  mainEntity: {
    "@type": "Person",
    name: "Maurizio Turatti",
    url: "https://maurizioturatti.com/",
    jobTitle: "Architecture Advisor and Company Co-Founder",
    worksFor: {
      "@type": "Organization",
      name: "SoftInstigate",
      url: "https://restheart.org",
    },
    alumniOf: {
      "@type": "EducationalOrganization",
      name: "Università degli Studi di Milano",
    },
  },
};
---

<Base
  title="About - Maurizio Turatti"
  description="Over two decades of making technical decisions and living with the results. Architecture advisory grounded in direct experience building and operating software."
  ogImage="/images/og-image.png"
  jsonLd={aboutJsonLd}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta
      name="keywords"
      content="Maurizio Turatti, architecture advisor, technical due diligence, CTO advisory, architectural decisions, software architecture"
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="hero hero--first">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="hero-headline">The decisions behind the systems.</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="page-content section-stack">
    <div class="section-block">
      <div class="section-body section-body--lead section-body--spacious">
        <p>
          Over two decades of technical decisions under incomplete information
          and unclear constraints. Understand the problem, surface the
          trade-offs that matter, make the call that keeps risk manageable.
        </p>
        <p>
          Co-founder of <a
            href="https://softinstigate.com"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">SoftInstigate</a
          > and creator of <a
            href="https://restheart.org"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">RESTHeart</a
          >, in production for 10+ years.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- How I work -->
    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">How I work</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="surface-card">
          <p class="card-label">Unclear systems and constraints</p>
          <p class="card-text">
            My work usually starts where the problem is still forming.
            Requirements are incomplete, stakeholders disagree on priorities,
            constraints are implicit, and the system is already running in
            production.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="surface-card">
          <p class="card-label">Decisions under pressure</p>
          <p class="card-text">
            Systems break when assumptions collide with production reality. The
            decisions that matter are the ones made with incomplete information,
            where the consequences of being wrong are visible and expensive.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="surface-card">
          <p class="card-label">Long-term consequences</p>
          <p class="card-text">
            Architecture decisions are difficult to undo. A choice that saves a
            month now can cost a year later. Each one carries the question: how
            hard will it be to change course if the assumptions were wrong?
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">AI adoption and architecture</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          AI is a multiplier of what is already there. It can accelerate
          development, and it can accelerate decay.
        </p>
        <p>
          AI follows a pattern: <strong>Envision</strong>, <strong>Experiment</strong>, <strong>Launch</strong>, <strong>Scale</strong>. Most startups and scale-ups are between Experiment and Launch. They have something working, but the architecture was built for speed, not for the load AI puts on it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The transition from pilot to production is where decisions become expensive to undo: what happens when the model changes, who owns output quality, how do you handle costs, what is the fallback when the AI is wrong.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Open source</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/restheart"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>RESTHeart</strong></a
          >: Agent-ready backend for MongoDB<br />
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/facet"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>Facet</strong></a
          >: Data-driven web framework: turn APIs into HTML, zero code<br />
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/ermes-mail"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>Ermes Mail</strong></a
          >: Async e-mail library and CLI for Java<br />
          <a href="https://github.com/mkjsix" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >All projects on GitHub →</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Teaching</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          Created and delivered technical courses and workshops for enterprise
          clients and partner networks across Italy and EMEA. Teaching forced me
          to articulate why certain decisions are made, which sharpened my own
          judgment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Writing</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          <a href="/writing/the-system-is-working"
            ><strong>The system is working. That is the problem.</strong></a
          >
          (Jun 2026)<br />
          <a
            href="https://medium.com/softinstigate-team/facet-a-different-approach-to-web-development-af884abe0b69"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            ><strong>Facet: A Different Approach to Web Development</strong></a
          >
          (Jan 2026)<br />
          <a
            href="https://medium.com/softinstigate-team/mongodb-deprecates-data-api-and-https-endpoints-how-restheart-can-help-58ea0c44660d"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            ><strong>MongoDB Deprecates Data API: How RESTHeart Can Help</strong
            ></a
          >
          (Feb 2025)
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ContactCta subtext="info@maurizioturatti.com" />
</Base>
